   "encoding": "Mark-Jan Nederhof, HieroJax text page 'British Museum EA581', https://nederhof.github.io/hierojax/texts/BritishMuseumEA581.html (fetched 2026-11-21); HieroJax repository is GPL-3.0",
   "direction": "Line direction from the same editor's RES encoding in the St Andrews corpus (PhilologEg 0.5.14, corpus/resources/IntefSonSenetHi.xml, created 2016-08-04, modified 2017-01-19): hrl = horizontal right-to-left, vrl = vertical right-to-left. Transcribed from a British Museum photograph, with Sethe (1928), Aegyptische Lesestuecke, pp. 80-81.",
   "note": "Encoding of relative positions is the editor's; it is not a facsimile."
  }
 },
 "rule": "tools/quadrat_census.py: a node is an operator application of arity >= 2\n(vertical joiner, horizontal joiner, insertion, overlay). Enclosures (cartouches, U+1343C/D)\nare parsed (HieroJax grammar, \"enclosure\") but the enclosure itself is not counted as a node;\nnodes inside an enclosure are counted separately and left out of the main comparison.",
 "tests": "(both one-sided: columns have the larger share of horizontal joins):\n  exact line-label permutation: all ways of choosing which lines are columns, keeping the\n     number of column lines fixed; statistic = pooled hor share in columns - in rows.\n     Lines, not nodes, are the units, because nodes in one line are not independent.\n  Fisher's exact test on the 2x2 node table, for comparison only (treats nodes as independent).",
